{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c44f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07303-b963-7e21-81f8-bb3541dfba40"},"sequence":130,"recorded_at":1780531400000255,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"19e64aa2-5eb1-4345-85e5-fc361fc0d256","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"19e64aa2-5eb1-4345-85e5-fc361fc0d256","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"19e64aa2-5eb1-4345-85e5-fc361fc0d256"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"60e7b8be-744f-4d51-ab89-d398c1382e41"},"task_id":"60e7b8be-744f-4d51-ab89-d398c1382e41","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"60e7b8be-744f-4d51-ab89-d398c1382e41","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-7-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board --help 2>&1 | head -n 60\\necho \\\"===\\\"\\ntask-board spawn --help 2>&1 | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect task-board CLI capabilities\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Manage a file-based task board with epics, stories, tasks, and bugs.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  admin                  Server administration (users, tokens, access)\\n  boards                 List boards accessible to the current user (remote mode)\\n  claude                 Launch Claude through the Task-board Session Manager\\n  codex                  Attach Codex to the Task-board Session Manager\\n  completion             Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\\n  export                 Export current board into a tar.gz archive\\n  goal                   Read and align the board-scoped parent primary goal\\n  grep                   Full-text search across board files\\n  handoff                Verify role handoff evidence and move to the role end status\\n  help                   Help about any command\\n  import                 Import a tar.gz archive into the current board\\n  limits                 Inspect and control provider rate-limit state\\n  login                  Store a token for the current remote\\n  logout                 Remove active user's token for current remote\\n  m                      Execute a mutation (write operation)\\n  migrate-keychain       Import legacy remote credentials into macOS Keychain\\n  migrate-project-config Preview or apply guarded deprecated project-config alias migration\\n  plan                   Show execution plan with phases and critical path\\n  q                      Query the board with a mini DSL\\n  repair-links           List or remove unsupported container dependency links\\n  resource               Upload, update, download, and delete board resources\\n  self-update            Update task-board to the latest version\\n  session                Inspect and stop Task-board Session Manager sessions\\n  spawn                  Queue an agent spawn run for a board task\\n  switch-user            Switch active user for current remote\\n  tree                   Show board as hierarchical tree\\n  tui                    Launch interactive TUI\\n  validate               Validate board structure\\n  whoami                 Show current remote and active user\\n  worktree               Inspect and repair managed Story workspaces\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n  -h, --help                     help for task-board\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n  -v, --version                  version for task-board\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n===\\nQueue an AI agent run (agy, claude, codex, gemini, muse, or qwen) for a board element.\\n\\nspawn.preferred_agentic_system is an optional provider allow-set. exclusive\\npins one provider; mixed retains runtime affinity when it belongs to the set or\\naccepts an explicit in-set --agent. Out-of-set providers are refused before\\ntask lookup or launch side effects. Legacy spawn.preferred_agent retains its\\nbest-effort preference behavior. Runtime affinity detects Codex from\\nCODEX_SESSION, CODEX_THREAD_ID, or CODEX_CI and otherwise selects Claude.\\nOptional spawn.schedule UTC windows temporarily replace the base provider set.\\nA provider or registered model outside the active window is refused before\\nside effects with the allowed set and a concrete retry step; the selected\\nprovider's ceiling is applied afterward.\\n\\nOn launch: assigns element to agent name, sets status from role config and\\nqueues a tracked background RUN. By default the public command returns\\nimmediately with observation commands. Pass --wait to block in the same process\\nuntil the RUN reaches a terminal state; no separate 'task-board spawn wait\\nRUN-...' invocation is needed. The --background flag is required so execution placement is explicit\\nat every callsite.\\n\\nPrompt composition:\\n  Primary source of truth is the board:\\n    - Task description comes from the element README\\n    - Task-specific DoD comes from the element checklist\\n    - Instructions come from precondition resources attached to the element\\n\\n  Legacy compatibility overrides:\\n    --task-path FILE  Optional extra brief appended to the task description\\n    --dod-path FILE   Optional extra DoD lines appended to the prompt only\\n\\nThe prompt is always composed from the role template plus board state. Legacy\\nfile overrides only append extra context — they never replace role identity,\\nboard task context, FIRST/LAST status blocks, skills, or CLI reference.\\n\\nSafety:\\n  --instruction NAME  Validates that a precondition resource matching NAME\\n                      is linked to the task before spawning. Errors with a\\n                      helpful message if not found.\\n\\nPrompt file is auto-saved to .temp/prompts/ with timestamp naming.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5158,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1290,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
