{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c63b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07303-b963-7e21-81f8-bb3541dfba40"},"sequence":376,"recorded_at":1780531400000747,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"19e64aa2-5eb1-4345-85e5-fc361fc0d256","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"19e64aa2-5eb1-4345-85e5-fc361fc0d256","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"19e64aa2-5eb1-4345-85e5-fc361fc0d256"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"bccafd2f-e1fd-4e20-87e7-8b753a45edeb"},"task_id":"bccafd2f-e1fd-4e20-87e7-8b753a45edeb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"bccafd2f-e1fd-4e20-87e7-8b753a45edeb","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-21-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff 57afcc6 2512f20 -- LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Show sibling story LOGBOOK additions\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex b8e9501..cb32048 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -3,6 +3,48 @@\\n > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n > Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-05\\n+\\n+### 0022 — Leaf-2 round-1 rework: refusal arms that share one code need clause assertions, not code assertions\\n+\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 rework after CHANGES REQUESTED (F1–F5, F9, G-A blocking; F6–F8 non-blocking). Production: `CheckOperation` admits `manifest`/`probe` with no capability dependency (§4.D); dead probe-identity branch and subsumed platform-dup check removed; `checkEvidenceSet` doc corrected to whole-reconciliation refusal. Tests: every refusal assertion in `manifest_test.go`/`manifest_pin_test.go` now names `*Error.Detail` (was 0/29); four over-determined `TestReconcileRefusals` fixtures narrowed until only the named rule rejects; `ParseProbe`/`ParseEvidence` gain the schema/version/identity/kind/digest cases only `ParseManifest` had; `now == expires_at` boundary row added.\\n+- STRUCTURAL ROOT: ~110 of 121 arms return `CodeMismatch`, so deleting a gate slides its fixture onto a lower arm and a code-only suite stays green. Against the narrowed fixtures all six re-runs (4 arm-shift gates + record-digest + expiry-boundary) fail with `error = <nil>`: the deleted gate admits what it must reject, and no lower arm catches the fixture.\\n+- F1 (live spec violation): `CheckOperation(\\\"manifest\\\"|\\\"probe\\\")` refused `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` even fully admitted; §4.D gives both `Capability dependencies: none` and neither row allows that code. Pinned by `TestCheckOperationAdmitsDependencyFreeOperations` (empty + full admitted sets, plus the still-refused gated operation).\\n+- F3 NARROWING SHAPE: the AdmitProbe substitution fixture now tracks the foreign digest in the probe, so probe↔manifest identity holds and only the manifest↔record gate can refuse. Same-shape-different-arm cases are indistinguishable by any assertion when both arms share code AND detail — the fixture, not the assertion, must isolate the arm.\\n+- G-A: new white-box `TestParsedClaimSlicesShareNoRegistryBacking` scribbles `REVIEW-POISON` into every parsed claim slice and re-reads the interior (row snapshot, `CapabilitiesForOperation`, fresh admission). The reviewer's positive control (return row slices from `parseClaim`) fails this pin while the old `TestAdmittedSharesNoBackingArrays` passed — that test touched three fields that cannot alias the table and never re-read the interior.\\n+- EVIDENCE: reviewer batteries re-run — battery-1 46 killed/0 survived (12 formulation-compile-fails covered by battery-2's compilable variants, all killed; M37/M58 re-anchored after the F1/F8 edits, both killed); battery-2 43 killed with exactly the 4 expected survivors (M71/M72 JCS unprovable with ASCII-only closed schemas — reported as bound, not coverage; M92/M95 near-equivalents). Targeted re-verification of all 24 fix mutants: 24/24 killed, each grep-confirmed present, compiling, and reverted.\\n+- F9: README `15.3#3` re-scoped (the prohibition is on advertising Structured Error as a capability; the admission registry is never on a hello path, clause stays undischarged), new `terminal-manifest-probe-admission` acceptance case registered, projection digest re-pinned, README figure 74→75 acceptance cases.\\n+- STATUS: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 rework, handed to review.\\n+\\n+## 2026-09-04\\n+\\n+### 2340 — Terminal manifest/probe/capability-evidence admission (leaf 2): mutant protocol caught a mis-targeted expiry test\\n+\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 on leaf-1 checkpoint `9481a20`. New: `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` (closed Manifest/Probe/Evidence schemas, 16-row capability registry, generation digest, rule 1–6 reconciliation, expiry, signature-verifier seam, operation gate, `Registry.AdmitProbe`); tests `manifest_test.go` (black-box, independent JCS/identity/RSA-signing recipe) + `manifest_pin_test.go` (white-box for parse-unreachable arms). Leaf-1 files touched only for a doc line and 3 added wire codes; no gate logic changed.\\n+- MUTANT PROTOCOL CAUGHT A MIS-TARGETED TEST: the \\\"expired evidence\\\" case re-signed mutated evidence (new ID) without refreshing the probe's `evidence_ids`, so under the original code it failed at liveness first (right arm, wrong reason to trust), and under a neutered-liveness mutant it failed at the ID-set arm instead of admitting — the test passed for the wrong reason and the mutant survived. Fix: every evidence-mutating case now calls `finalizeProbeIDs` after re-signing (6 cases + platform case), so each refusal lands on its intended arm; the corrected liveness mutant is killed.\\n+- DETERMINISTIC SIGNATURES DEDUP: RSA PKCS1v15 is deterministic per key+message, so a \\\"distinct extra evidence\\\" fixture built with identical fields was byte-identical and correctly deduplicated — the test was wrong, production right. Unreferenced-object case now varies a supplementary fact (`ui_absent`) to force distinct bytes; identical-duplicate acceptance is pinned white-box as the stated bound.\\n+- REAL PRODUCTION BUG FOUND BY TEST: strict decoder returned nil (not empty) slices for `[]`, so `json.Marshal` re-encoded them as `null` and omit-self identity recomputation diverged on claim-free/evidence-free documents. Fixed with non-nil array initialization; pinned by the empty-tuple admission test.\\n+- EVIDENCE: board outcome artifact `TASK-260830-1zvmw7_manifest-probe-evidence.md` — 12/12 mutants killed (each grep-confirmed present, compiling, red, reverted byte-identical), suite/vet/gofmt/tracecheck exit 0, package coverage 87.1%.\\n+\\n+### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\\n+\\n+- SCOPE: rework of TASK-260830-2xdt8t after CHANGES REQUESTED (five blocking findings F1–F5). Production: `internal/terminalbackend` clones slices on ingress (`New` per-builtin copy, `RegisterExternal` store copy) and egress (`Resolve` return copy). No new refusal sites.\\n+- F1: `Resolve` returned the struct by value with shared backing arrays, `RegisterExternal` stored the caller record verbatim, `New` shared one protocol array across both built-ins — an in-place mutation converted drift into `terminal_backend_ambiguous` and the registry adopted the change. Pinned by `TestRegistryCopiesSlicesAcrossItsBoundary` (four subtests, incl. the end-to-end duplicate-instead-of-drift bypass).\\n+- F2: drift table gains same-length cases (`[\\\"1.0.0\\\"]→[\\\"1.1.0\\\"]`, `[linux]→[macos]`); the length-changing cases alone left the member loops deletable.\\n+- F3: generation-bound test rewritten with EQUAL generations on both sides (1 and 256 admitted; 0 and 257 refused); mismatch arm split into `TestCheckProviderDescriptorGenerationMismatch`. The old test proved the inequality, not the bound.\\n+- F4: `validatePlatforms` fully narrowed (dup/empty/unknown/5-list, with the 5-list asserting the `platforms bound` clause since any 5-list over the 4-member vocabulary also fails a later rule); protocol `[1..32]` bound pinned with 33 distinct sorted members plus 32-member admission; `DigestFile` FIFO case pins the `IsRegular` guard (the directory case is EISDIR-confounded); trust-loop `ParseID` pinned against deletion by the `INVALID_ID` wiring case.\\n+- EQUIVALENT MUTANTS (documented, not covered): reverting the trust-loop `ParseID` to the previous local pattern is behavior-identical — same refusal set, intentionally non-distinguishing clause, `ax.` difference subsumed by the `HasPrefix` line two statements later. `parseKind`'s vocabulary arm and the digest-must-be-null arm are unreachable through current entry points (external-kind gate precedes validation with `Untrusted`, pinned by `TestRegisterExternalRefusesUnknownKindAsUntrusted`); measured white-box in `internal_pin_test.go` with the reachability bound stated.\\n+- F5: `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` registered in `config-versioned-readers`; ownership projection digest re-pinned; README discharge prose names both arms. No figure moved (74 cases, 17/403).\\n+- EVIDENCE: `TASK-260830-2xdt8t_rework-verification.md` (board outcome artifact) with the mutation re-run ratio.\\n+\\n+### 2147 — Terminal backend registry: the two board-disclosed findings decided without inventing constraints\\n+\\n+- SCOPE: new `internal/terminalbackend/` (registry, canonical IDs, version tuples, trust, duplicate/drift refusal, restore binding, §7.A descriptor check), `internal/config/validation.go` wiring, new `internal/config/terminal_registry_wiring_test.go`. TASK-260830-2xdt8t, spec v0.5.0 §4.B, §4.1, §6.5, §7.A. Signed commit on story branch, worktree clean, not pushed.\\n+- DECISION (finding 1): `required_capabilities` keeps its empty default. SPEC.md:2585 (\\\"default platform lane minimum\\\") is the sole occurrence of the phrase in the 12,665-line SPEC; no per-platform minimum set is enumerated anywhere, so implementing one would invent a constraint. STATED BOUND (review correction to this entry's earlier reasoning): the clause is underspecified, so empty is the only non-inventing default — and the choice is recorded as underspecification, not as a neutral default, because `required_capabilities` restricts and empty is therefore the weaker gate. The earlier appeal to SPEC.md:2604-2605 did not carry the argument and is withdrawn. No code change; audit finding recorded as ANSWERED.\\n+- DECISION (finding 2): §6.2 \\\"terminal backend MUST be conpty\\\" on native Windows (SPEC.md:2415-2418) governs the v1/v2 `terminal.backend` field and is enforced across versions; added the missing legacy-arm pin `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` (v1 tmux-on-Windows refuses, conpty loads to `ax.conpty`). Deliberately NOT extended to third-party IDs: §6.5 admits them as \\\"valid registered ID\\\" with manifest-bound platforms.\\n+- EVIDENCE: `go test ./...` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean; terminalbackend 89.3%, config 94.7% statement coverage. Every refusal gate narrowed (grammar widened one rule at a time; drift changes one record member at a time); `TestErrorPredicatesAreExclusive` proves one wire code per refusal; duplicate/drift refusals assert the admitted record is unchanged. Wire codes verified against the pinned catalog vocabulary in-test.\\n+- BOUND: registry is process-local memory — no durable-state crash-recovery evidence applies; duplicate/drift non-clobber assertions are the idempotency evidence. Manifest/Probe schemas, capability evidence, lifecycle ops, legacy v0.4.3 translation are sibling tasks, untouched.\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-03\\n \\n ### 1632 — The generalisation was written down one round earlier and still not executed: a list is a forced traversal, prose is a memory\\n@@ -673,3 +715,47 @@ assertion here rather than a brittle one.\\n - NOTE: General property, applies to every derived gate — an inventory must assert that the set of constructs