green. Against the narrowed fixtures all six re-runs (4 arm-shift gates + record-digest + expiry-boundary) fail with `error = <nil>`: the deleted gate admits what it must reject, and no lower arm catches the fixture.\\n+- F1 (live spec violation): `CheckOperation(\\\"manifest\\\"|\\\"probe\\\")` refused `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` even fully admitted; §4.D gives both `Capability dependencies: none` and neither row allows that code. Pinned by `TestCheckOperationAdmitsDependencyFreeOperations` (empty + full admitted sets, plus the still-refused gated operation).\\n+- F3 NARROWING SHAPE: the AdmitProbe substitution fixture now tracks the foreign digest in the probe, so probe↔manifest identity holds and only the manifest↔record gate can refuse. Same-shape-different-arm cases are indistinguishable by any assertion when both arms share code AND detail — the fixture, not the assertion, must isolate the arm.\\n+- G-A: new white-box `TestParsedClaimSlicesShareNoRegistryBacking` scribbles `REVIEW-POISON` into every parsed claim slice and re-reads the interior (row snapshot, `CapabilitiesForOperation`, fresh admission). The reviewer's positive control (return row slices from `parseClaim`) fails this pin while the old `TestAdmittedSharesNoBackingArrays` passed — that test touched three fields that cannot alias the table and never re-read the interior.\\n+- EVIDENCE: reviewer batteries re-run — battery-1 46 killed/0 survived (12 formulation-compile-fails covered by battery-2's compilable variants, all killed; M37/M58 re-anchored after the F1/F8 edits, both killed); battery-2 43 killed with exactly the 4 expected survivors (M71/M72 JCS unprovable with ASCII-only closed schemas — reported as bound, not coverage; M92/M95 near-equivalents). Targeted re-verification of all 24 fix mutants: 24/24 killed, each grep-confirmed present, compiling, and reverted.\\n+- F9: README `15.3#3` re-scoped (the prohibition is on advertising Structured Error as a capability; the admission registry is never on a hello path, clause stays undischarged), new `terminal-manifest-probe-admission` acceptance case registered, projection digest re-pinned, README figure 74→75 acceptance cases.\\n+- STATUS: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 rework, handed to review.\\n+\\n+## 2026-09-04\\n+\\n+### 2340 — Terminal manifest/probe/capability-evidence admission (leaf 2): mutant protocol caught a mis-targeted expiry test\\n+\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 on leaf-1 checkpoint `9481a20`. New: `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` (closed Manifest/Probe/Evidence schemas, 16-row capability registry, generation digest, rule 1–6 reconciliation, expiry, signature-verifier seam, operation gate, `Registry.AdmitProbe`); tests `manifest_test.go` (black-box, independent JCS/identity/RSA-signing recipe) + `manifest_pin_test.go` (white-box for parse-unreachable arms). Leaf-1 files touched only for a doc line and 3 added wire codes; no gate logic changed.\\n+- MUTANT PROTOCOL CAUGHT A MIS-TARGETED TEST: the \\\"expired evidence\\\" case re-signed mutated evidence (new ID) without refreshing the probe's `evidence_ids`, so under the original code it failed at liveness first (right arm, wrong reason to trust), and under a neutered-liveness mutant it failed at the ID-set arm instead of admitting — the test passed for the wrong reason and the mutant survived. Fix: every evidence-mutating case now calls `finalizeProbeIDs` after re-signing (6 cases + platform case), so each refusal lands on its intended arm; the corrected liveness mutant is killed.\\n+- DETERMINISTIC SIGNATURES DEDUP: RSA PKCS1v15 is deterministic per key+message, so a \\\"distinct extra evidence\\\" fixture built with identical fields was byte-identical and correctly deduplicated — the test was wrong, production right. Unreferenced-object case now varies a supplementary fact (`ui_absent`) to force distinct bytes; identical-duplicate acceptance is pinned white-box as the stated bound.\\n+- REAL PRODUCTION BUG FOUND BY TEST: strict decoder returned nil (not empty) slices for `[]`, so `json.Marshal` re-encoded them as `null` and omit-self identity recomputation diverged on claim-free/evidence-free documents. Fixed with non-nil array initialization; pinned by the empty-tuple admission test.\\n+- EVIDENCE: board outcome artifact `TASK-260830-1zvmw7_manifest-probe-evidence.md` — 12/12 mutants killed (each grep-confirmed present, compiling, red, reverted byte-identical), suite/vet/gofmt/tracecheck exit 0, package coverage 87.1%.\\n+\\n+### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\\n+\\n+- SCOPE: rework of TASK-260830-2xdt8t after CHANGES REQUESTED (five blocking findings F1–F5). Production: `internal/terminalbackend` clones slices on ingress (`New` per-builtin copy, `RegisterExternal` store copy) and egress (`Resolve` return copy). No new refusal sites.\\n+- F1: `Resolve` returned the struct by value with shared backing arrays, `RegisterExternal` stored the caller record verbatim, `New` shared one protocol array across both built-ins — an in-place mutation converted drift into `terminal_backend_ambiguous` and the registry adopted the change. Pinned by `TestRegistryCopiesSlicesAcrossItsBoundary` (four subtests, incl. the end-to-end duplicate-instead-of-drift bypass).\\n+- F2: drift table gains same-length cases (`[\\\"1.0.0\\\"]→[\\\"1.1.0\\\"]`, `[linux]→[macos]`); the length-changing cases alone left the member loops deletable.\\n+- F3: generation-bound test rewritten with EQUAL generations on both sides (1 and 256 admitted; 0 and 257 refused); mismatch arm split into `TestCheckProviderDescriptorGenerationMismatch`. The old test proved the inequality, not the bound.\\n+- F4: `validatePlatforms` fully narrowed (dup/empty/unknown/5-list, with the 5-list asserting the `platforms bound` clause since any 5-list over the 4-member vocabulary also fails a later rule); protocol `[1..32]` bound pinned with 33 distinct sorted members plus 32-member admissi