-1 rework: refusal arms that share one code need clause assertions, not code assertions\\n101:## 2026-09-04\\n103:### 2340 — Terminal manifest/probe/capability-evidence admission (leaf 2): mutant protocol caught a mis-targeted expiry test\\n111:### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\\n122:### 2147 — Terminal backend registry: the two board-disclosed findings decided without inventing constraints\\n130:### 0230 — The guard the round did not sweep was the one that matters: uid 0 admitted, suite green\\n140:### 0210 — The inventory gate proves a site was reached, not that a test can tell which site fired\\n151:### 0115 — Provider discovery leaf: the inventory gate caught a test proving nothing, and a trust test caught a double hash\\n...\\n256:### 1003 — An exit status is a class, not an identity: the fan-in is 47 codes over 17 statuses, and no CLI process exists to produce either\\n275:### 1015 — encoding/json is not a validator: it substitutes U+FFFD for a byte the contract requires to be valid UTF-8\\n291:### 0753 — Validate-then-alias is a bypass path, not a gate; and a clause claimed against the wrong actor\\n305:### 0742 — A key-name blacklist, again: the same shape BUG-260902-2faftr removed, caught by reading the logbook rather than by a test\\n320:### 0626 — Third instance of one class in one comment: the pin proved the digit and never the noun\\n334:### 0559 — The fix for a false claim shipped a false citation, and the bound that let it through said \\\"unmeasurable\\\" where the package already measured\\n346:### 0553 — A doc comment that promises a refusal is only pinnable if the doc is the test's input\\n359:### 0412 — Symbol reachability is not semantic coverage, and 48 bindings measured 2/394\\n373:### 0900 — \\\"No RFC 2119 keyword\\\" is a failure to measure, not an absence of obligation\\n385:### 0210 — A derived call graph that only sees `f(x)` covers 3 of 7 guards and looks complete\\n396:### 0135 — The fidelity fix reproduced its own bug, one schema over\\n407:### 0050 — Correcting one gate's input silently narrowed another gate\\n425:### 0035 — Stale line numbers turned a four-site audit into an eight-site class\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3100,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 775,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
