runs. First, publication: there is no producer-side publish command by design — the completion-time finalizer snapshots this tree into the next revision (expected rev 8, same 60-path scope) when this run finalizes, then runs the validation suite. So the resulting revision number was not observable from inside the run; read it back with `task-board worktree status`. Files differing from accepted rev 7 will be exactly `LOGBOOK.md` and `README.md`. Second, the combination still needs its review pass (round 10, then `accept_cr`, then integrate) — and at integrate time, the `ownership.v0.5.0.json` overlap (trunk 74+3 disjoint sibling cases vs this tree 74+4 ours) must resolve to a 81-case union with the README figures lifted 78 → 81, or the pin test goes red on trunk. Both points are recorded in the attached outcome `TASK-260830-32jeti_merge-report.md`.","reason":null}}
